      "our_prose": "Central and south Florida are hard on thyme because it is a Mediterranean herb that hates the humid heat, which rots its roots. Grow it in a pot or raised bed with fast-draining soil, plant in the cooler months, choose a heat-tolerant upright type, and give afternoon shade. In central Florida a potted plant may last a few years; in the far south, treat it as a short-lived plant you replace.",
